{
  "inShort": "With no playable build or five-player notes to open, the team finishes behind: the checkpoint goal was missed. Sprint 4 added no artifacts, so what actually got finished is unknown. The reported islands, tide loop and co-op remain unproven, an evidence gap that can be closed next checkpoint.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvzgwd2l00k5kmz8u4ocak9l",
      "text": "A public repository of the Godot demo projects the game builds on is verified. It supplies source examples, not an openable build of your slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvzgwd3300k6kmz8rs96hp7n",
      "text": "An animated reference video for the art style remains done. Its title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny; the animation was not watched. Sprint 4 links that film again, not footage establishing the islands, tide loop or co-op. The mountain photograph does not demonstrate the tide either."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvzgwd4500k7kmz8lmxh6bq4",
      "text": "A reference article on what playtesting is, for the team to read is verified. It explains testing, but supplies no evidence of the reported five-player session or what players learned about the tide."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvzgwd4p00k8kmz8h7122ux3",
      "text": "A private design board for the team remains done. Its contents were not checked, so it does not establish a chosen style in this review."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "What did the five players’ actions establish about the tide loop and co-op sailing?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlog #1, Devlog #2, Devlog #3 and Devlog #4 reported progress, each receiving 0 applause and 0 views; no playable download or store link is listed.",
    "team": "Only Alex’s 10–15 weekly hours are stated, totaling 40–60 hours across the checkpoint. Alex confirmed all four weeks; Mia stopped confirming after week 1, leaving engineering capacity for the playable slice unverified.",
    "management": "The four completed reference tasks do not establish the playable core needed before release, although the checked prototype-devlog requirement passes the formal stage gate. For the next checkpoint, link the build, co-op instructions and five-player notes."
  }
}

